<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Qurra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Qurra was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-ifran">Banu Ifran</a>, a Zenata <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tribe of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berber-revolt">Berber revolts</a> against Arab rule. A Sufri Kharijite, he was proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> around 742 and founded the first Ifranid state. He raised large armies and joined attacks on Abbasid governors in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>, including the siege of Tubna in the 770s.</p></div>
